    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Optimize the memory locality and loop order in the given code.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Reorder the loops to reduce cache misses.\",\n    \"Use vectorization to improve performance.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"--- BEGIN FILE src/solution.cpp ---\\n#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n,s;\\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\\n    std::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)\\n        for(int j=0;j<n;j++) \\n            scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n    assert(s<n);\\n    assert(n<8000);\\n    assert(s>0);\\n    assert(n>0);\\n\\n    int sum = 0;\\n    for(int i=0;i<s;i++)\\n        for(int j=0;j<s;j++)\\n            sum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\n    int mxSum = sum;\\n\\n    int dir = 1;\\n    int i = 0;\\n    int j = 0;\\n    while(i+s <= n) {\\n        if( (j+s == n && dir==1) || (j==0 && dir==-1) ) { \\n            int exitingRow = i;\\n            int enteringRow = exitingRow+s;\\n            if(enteringRow >=n) break;\\n\\n            for(int k=0;k<s;k++) { sum -= matrix[exitingRow][k+j]; } \\n            for(int k=0;k<s;k++) { sum += matrix[enteringRow][k+j]; } \\n\\n            i++;\\n            dir*=-1;\\n        } else {\\n            int exitingCol,enteringCol;\\n            if(dir==1) {\\n                exitingCol = j;\\n                enteringCol = exitingCol + s;\\n            } else {\\n                enteringCol = j-1;\\n                exitingCol = enteringCol + s;\\n            }\\n\\n            for(int k=0;k<s;k++) {sum -= matrix[k+i][exitingCol]; } \\n            for(int k=0;k<s;k++) {sum += matrix[k+i][enteringCol]; } \\n            j+=dir;\\n        }\\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum,sum);\\n    }\\n    printf(\\\"%d\\n\\\",mxSum);\\n}\\n--- END FILE src/solution.cpp ---\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The current code has a nested loop structure that can lead to cache misses and inefficiencies. By reordering the loops and using vectorization, we can improve the performance of the code.\",\n  \"research\": {\n    \"queries\": [\n      \"How can we optimize the memory locality in a nested loop?\",\n      \"What are the benefits of using vectorization in a loop?\",\n      \"How can we reduce cache misses in a nested loop?\"\n    ],\n    \"urls\": [\n      \"https://www.cs.umd.edu/class/2019spring/cs106/notes/09-vectorization.pdf\",\n      \"https://www.cs.umd.edu/class/2019spring/cs106/notes/10-cache-misses.pdf\"\n    ]\n  }\n}"
